// expect: 134
// EXPECTATION TRUED (2026-07-25, the resolved-or-loud offset landing): the
// old banked value was the PARTIAL-SET offset read — the arm's demanded
// {beta | rho} summed offsets over {beta} alone, so .beta read offset 0,
// the receiver's first SORTED field (alpha). resolve_field_offset now
// resolves the full set through the row residual or floors LOUDLY; this
// arm's rho is genuinely free (the op param is polymorphic across
// performs), so the trap is the honest answer until arm specialization
// (the spec-twin machinery at handler arms) closes the payload residual.
// Bottom-up probe of the ONE primitive: does ~> read the performed value's
// type into the handler arm? No map, no buffer, no iterate. emit carries a
// record; the arm reads v.beta. If the payload edge works, v : the record,
// v.beta = 2 (sorted alpha=0,beta=1,gamma=2 -> offset 4). If the arm re-derives
// a fresh var (the drift, foreign-fluency "fresh per binding"), v.beta traps.
effect Probe {
  emit(x) -> Int
}

handler collect {
  emit(v) => resume(v.beta)
}

fn run() with Probe + Memory + Alloc = emit({alpha: 1, beta: 2, gamma: 3})

fn main(q) = run() ~> collect
